Chris waters here with a gamespot news  update we spoke to the developers of the  infamous series who said that the game  originally had a lot in common with  nintendo's animal crossing the  co-founder of Sucker Punch productions  chris zimmerman told GameSpot the  original idea for infamous believe it or  not was that it was a kind of animal  crossing but you were a superhero one of  the game's original pitches had players  fighting a gang of purple gorillas who  were stealing balloons zimmerman  explained we had all kinds of crazy  stuff like that we worked on that for  about a year it was much more stylized  much more cartoony than what you end up  seeing we worked hard to see if we could  make that work unfortunately we don't  have any images of this very early  version of infamous to share and  obviously the final game ended up going  in a very different direction the next  installment of the infamous series is  second son which launches on March 21st  exclusively for the PlayStation 4 for  more information on infamous second son  be sure to check out GameSpot's just  published coverage from our trip to  sucker punch productions
 

